{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The self-drilling screws and lag-bolt assortment fit my ongoing fastening work: one supports sheet-metal repairs, while the other adds larger sizes for heavier wood connections.",
    "The clamp meter extends my inspection and measurement tools into electrical troubleshooting, while duct tape and B-7000 glue offer useful repair options alongside my existing tapes and epoxy."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The CO2 monitor measures something, but indoor air monitoring does not serve the hands-on repair needs behind my recent measuring-tool purchases. The tourniquets likewise address a need I have not expressed.",
    "Pocket-hole screws and printer heater parts require a particular project or compatible equipment I have not indicated. A hundred identical M3 screws also feel premature without a matching size requirement."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying several measuring tools seems to have been taken as interest in any monitoring device, regardless of what I need to inspect or repair.",
    "My frequent fastener purchases seem to have been treated as interest in almost any screw, even when its application or dimensions are too specific for my current needs."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly choose assortments with multiple sizes, which help me handle varied repairs; a large pack of one exact size offers less flexibility without a known requirement.",
    "Useful next choices either extend a repair capability I already use or complement my existing supplies. Equipment-specific replacements need evidence that I own the matching equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my ongoing repair work, but sometimes mistake broad tool similarity for a practical next need."
}"}
